WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.066
We’ll be able to see it from the top of the hill!

2
00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.199
- All right!
- Pikachu!

3
00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.900
-Ha-ha!

4
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:16.633
- Smell the ocean!
- It feels so nice!

5
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.166
It’s always great to get to the shore!

6
00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:21.733
This says how beautiful Ambrette Town is!

7
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.233
- That’s the ocean, Dedenne!
- Na! Na! Na!

8
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:30.333
All right, Froakie, I choose you!

9
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.366
- Check out the ocean!
- Froakie!

10
00:00:35.066 --> 00:00:38.433
Froakie’s a Water type, no wonder it’s so happy!

11
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.333
Yeah. This would be a great spot to train!

12
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.100
But there’s still somewhere I want to go.

13
00:00:44.166 --> 00:00:45.500
Where’s that, Serena?

14
00:00:45.566 --> 00:00:49.366
- Ta-da! Ambrette Aquarium!
- Aquarium?

15
00:00:49.433 --> 00:00:53.766
Great! It’s got lots of Water-type Pokémon from all the different regions!

16
00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:56.866
That’s it! I’ve wanted to go since forever!

17
00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:01.266
- Sounds like fun! I’d like to go, too!
- Pika, Pika!

18
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:03.433
I want to go! I want to go! I want to go!

19
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.933
Then... let’s go!

20
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.733
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

21
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.533
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

22
00:01:12.566 --> 00:01:15.133
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

23
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

24
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.233
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

25
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.533
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

26
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

27
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

28
00:01:30.433 --> 00:01:32.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

29
00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:35.933
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

30
00:01:44.966 --> 00:01:47.800
Continuing their journey to Cyllage City,

31
00:01:47.866 --> 00:01:50.800
our heroes have decided to visit Ambrette Aquarium,

32
00:01:50.866 --> 00:01:54.699
where they can marvel at the many Water-type Pokémon on display there!

33
00:01:54.766 --> 00:01:58.066
Welcome to Ambrette Aquarium.

34
00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:01.466
I’m sure you’ll enjoy all our aquatic displays!

35
00:02:01.533 --> 00:02:03.199
Can’t wait to see them!

36
00:02:03.266 --> 00:02:07.533
Our aquarium is the perfect place to see many different Water-type Pokémon.

37
00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.799
You’re a keeper! Wow!

38
00:02:10.866 --> 00:02:14.033
Hey! I need you to take care of my brother, please!

39
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.100
Bonnie, I told you to stop this a million times!

40
00:02:20.566 --> 00:02:22.833
This is so embarrassing.

41
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.799
I hope you’ll think about it, please!

42
00:02:25.866 --> 00:02:28.533
Have a nice day!

43
00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.266
-Pika!

44
00:02:34.333 --> 00:02:37.533
- Wow, so many!
- Pikachu!

45
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.400
They’re beautiful!

46
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.700
Wow!

47
00:02:43.766 --> 00:02:45.233
A Gorebyss! Wow!

48
00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:49.333
It’s a pink Pokémon and it’s totally cute! Incredible!

49
00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.533
That scared me!

50
00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.299
That’s a Relicanth.

51
00:02:58.366 --> 00:03:01.400
- Did that scare you too, Dedenne?
- Na-na-na-na.

52
00:03:05.966 --> 00:03:09.533
- Cool! Stunfisk!
- Pika, Pika!

53
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.166
Stunkfisk!

54
00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:15.433
- Woo-hoo!
- You mean Wooper.

55
00:03:16.566 --> 00:03:19.233
- Clamperl!
- Too cute!

56
00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.799
- Lanturn!
- Pika!

57
00:03:22.866 --> 00:03:24.433
They’re beautiful!

58
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:28.266
- Aren’t they pretty, Dedenne?
- Na! Na!

59
00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:30.266
It’s like we’re all underwater.

60
00:03:30.333 --> 00:03:33.466
You never get to see Water-type Pokémon from this angle.

61
00:03:33.533 --> 00:03:35.033
- What a treat!
- Yeah, right!

62
00:03:36.166 --> 00:03:38.333
- Hey, what’s that?
- It’s a Mantine!

63
00:03:38.399 --> 00:03:41.066
- Awesome!
- It’s gigantic!

64
00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:45.133
Whoever designed this aquarium sure knows a lot about Water-type Pokémon!

65
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.666
- For sure!
- Pikachu!

66
00:03:48.866 --> 00:03:52.566
And now here’s a group of Piplup out for a little stroll.

67
00:03:52.633 --> 00:03:54.433
Piplup!

68
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.066
- Cutie pie!
- Whoops! Wrong way!

69
00:03:57.133 --> 00:04:00.766
- Pip, Pip, Pip!
- Piplup are really friendly, aren’t they?

70
00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:03.600
Pikachu and I know a Piplup who’s really something else!

71
00:04:03.666 --> 00:04:05.399
Pikachu!

72
00:04:05.466 --> 00:04:06.933
Piplup!

73
00:04:08.166 --> 00:04:10.500
- Hey, it’s a Magikarp!
- Pika!

74
00:04:10.566 --> 00:04:12.233
Karp!

75
00:04:12.299 --> 00:04:14.066
Magikarp, the Fish Pokémon.

76
00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:16.800
Because all Magikarp seem to do is splash around,

77
00:04:16.866 --> 00:04:20.000
some consider them weak, but they’re actually a hardy Pokémon

78
00:04:20.066 --> 00:04:22.533
that can survive in water no matter how dirty it is.

79
00:04:22.599 --> 00:04:24.366
-Magikarp!

80
00:04:24.433 --> 00:04:26.400
They do splash around a lot.

81
00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:30.166
You know, many Magikarp live in the bay here.

82
00:04:30.233 --> 00:04:31.800
Uh... Who are you?

83
00:04:31.866 --> 00:04:34.033
Just a friendly observer.

84
00:04:34.099 --> 00:04:37.466
Of course there are many different types of Pokémon in the world,

85
00:04:37.533 --> 00:04:41.633
but Water-type Pokémon are surprisingly the second most common type.

86
00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.066
-I never knew that!

87
00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.733
Pika, Pika!

88
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.800
See, there are so many different types of Water-type Pokémon

89
00:04:48.866 --> 00:04:51.633
because they have adapted to the many different environments

90
00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.033
that are found in the ocean.

91
00:04:53.099 --> 00:04:55.633
- Man, that’s cool stuff!
- Ah!

92
00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:58.300
- Did you see outside?
- Uh, see what?

93
00:04:58.366 --> 00:04:59.466
Pika?

94
00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:03.666
I meant this!

95
00:05:04.666 --> 00:05:07.000
-Huh? A Magikarp statue!

96
00:05:07.066 --> 00:05:10.099
- And it’s gold colored.
- It’s so big!

97
00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:16.333
It’s a statue of the giant golden Magikarp.

98
00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.866
So, why did they make a statue for it?

99
00:05:18.933 --> 00:05:22.933
This Magikarp represents a dream for a lot of people.

100
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.866
If you’d like to learn more,

101
00:05:24.933 --> 00:05:27.866
I suggest you speak to that gentleman over there.

102
00:05:27.933 --> 00:05:30.500
You see, he’s the aquarium’s curator!

103
00:05:31.733 --> 00:05:36.133
I must be going now. He has great stories to tell.

104
00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.666
Thanks very much!

105
00:05:37.733 --> 00:05:40.400
- Well, let’s go!
- Mm-hm!

106
00:05:40.466 --> 00:05:42.900
Hm?

107
00:05:44.566 --> 00:05:45.700
Hm?

108
00:05:46.833 --> 00:05:49.466
Dig it! Swiping and selling that gold statue

109
00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:51.333
should make us beaucoup de bucks!

110
00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:55.033
Don’t count our millions just yet. It’s probably just gold-plated.

111
00:05:55.099 --> 00:05:59.933
Agreed. If it was solid gold, it simply wouldn’t be out here, unprotected.

112
00:06:00.066 --> 00:06:02.566
If that’s true, why would they have a statue like this

113
00:06:02.633 --> 00:06:04.533
hanging out here in the first place?

114
00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:08.266
Perhaps there’s a real giant golden Magikarp splashing somewhere out there.

115
00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:10.766
It behooves us to make it ours, then.

116
00:06:17.433 --> 00:06:20.466
Hm. Yes! A bite!

117
00:06:20.533 --> 00:06:23.366
It’s a big one, that’s for sure!

118
00:06:23.433 --> 00:06:26.633
- Huh?

119
00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.533
Oh!

120
00:06:28.599 --> 00:06:29.900
Oh!

121
00:06:29.966 --> 00:06:31.633
Excuse me, do you run the aquarium?

122
00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.766
Why, yes, I do. My name is Rodman.

123
00:06:34.833 --> 00:06:39.200
Nice to meet you. I’d also like you to meet my partner, Clauncher.

124
00:06:39.266 --> 00:06:40.766
Clauncher, Clauncher!

125
00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.866
- Pika!
- It’s a Clauncher!

126
00:06:44.666 --> 00:06:46.700
Clauncher, the Water Gun Pokémon.

127
00:06:46.766 --> 00:06:50.066
Clauncher fires compressed water from the arm gun on its right claw

128
00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:52.400
and damages foes with the impact from the water.

129
00:06:52.466 --> 00:06:54.099
Clauncher!

130
00:06:54.166 --> 00:06:56.133
- Whoa!
- Pikachu!

131
00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.299
We were curious about that giant golden Magikarp statue.

132
00:06:59.366 --> 00:07:01.966
Oh, that statue’s amazing, isn’t it?

133
00:07:02.033 --> 00:07:06.599
As a matter of fact, I’m trying to catch the real golden Magikarp right now!

134
00:07:06.666 --> 00:07:09.099
-There’s a real golden Magikarp?

135
00:07:09.166 --> 00:07:13.066
Mm! According to local legend, yes.

136
00:07:13.133 --> 00:07:16.466
So that explains why that amazing statue’s on display!

137
00:07:19.233 --> 00:07:21.666
The legend’s been around for years.

138
00:07:23.666 --> 00:07:27.066
Long ago, people spent lots of time free diving here.

139
00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:30.599
One day, a free diver was shocked by a Starmie while underwater

140
00:07:30.666 --> 00:07:33.400
and came very close to drowning.

141
00:07:33.466 --> 00:07:37.933
Suddenly, a mysterious giant golden Magikarp appeared out of nowhere

142
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:42.400
and carried the free diver to shore, saving his life.

143
00:07:42.466 --> 00:07:43.733
Wow!

144
00:07:43.799 --> 00:07:48.000
Apparently, the giant golden Magikarp has been spotted in this same area

145
00:07:48.066 --> 00:07:50.500
- several other times.
- Fascinating.

146
00:07:50.566 --> 00:07:55.433
You see, the mayor is a very friendly man, so when I told him about the legend,

147
00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.000
he installed that golden Magikarp statue for the aquarium.

148
00:07:59.066 --> 00:08:01.299
My dream is to catch it for the aquarium,

149
00:08:01.366 --> 00:08:04.700
so children will have the opportunity to see it up close.

150
00:08:04.766 --> 00:08:08.000
That way, everyone will enjoy the aquarium even more.

151
00:08:08.066 --> 00:08:13.066
After all, the purpose of an aquarium is to educate and entertain, don’t you think?

152
00:08:13.133 --> 00:08:15.599
Sounds really awesome to me!

153
00:08:15.666 --> 00:08:17.299
- Pika!
- Huh? Huh?

154
00:08:18.633 --> 00:08:20.599
Pika? Pika, Pika!

155
00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:22.299
- Clan!
- Pika?

156
00:08:28.666 --> 00:08:30.866
Well, well, well...

157
00:08:30.933 --> 00:08:32.166
It’s a legend!

158
00:08:32.233 --> 00:08:35.066
Where there’s smoke, there’s fire, I always say.

159
00:08:35.133 --> 00:08:36.966
Which means, if it is real...

160
00:08:37.033 --> 00:08:38.366
We’ll swim in success!

161
00:08:38.433 --> 00:08:41.933
Then Operation Catch the Golden Magikarp is under way!

162
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.100
Oh! I just had a big brainstorm! Pedal to the metal!

163
00:08:46.166 --> 00:08:48.199
Full speed ahead!

164
00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:55.166
Oh! I got a bite!

165
00:08:55.233 --> 00:08:56.900
Wow, this could be it!

166
00:08:56.966 --> 00:08:58.433
The golden Magikarp!

167
00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.033
It’s a big one!

168
00:09:03.766 --> 00:09:05.633
Whoa!

169
00:09:05.699 --> 00:09:09.433
- Karp Magikarp!
- Aw!

170
00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:14.000
- Karp?
- Oh! It’s just a regular Magikarp.

171
00:09:14.066 --> 00:09:15.233
- Oh!

172
00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.300
Karp! Magikarp!

173
00:09:17.366 --> 00:09:21.766
Whenever I catch a regular Magikarp, I always release it back into the ocean.

174
00:09:21.833 --> 00:09:23.833
Oh!

175
00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.433
I know! I’ll help you catch it!

176
00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.666
- Me, too!
- I’d like to help, too!

177
00:09:28.733 --> 00:09:32.766
Well, looks like I’ve got myself a fishing team!

178
00:09:32.833 --> 00:09:35.100
Here!

179
00:09:35.166 --> 00:09:39.566
No doubt I’m going to be the one who catches that giant golden Magikarp!

180
00:09:39.633 --> 00:09:42.366
- We’ll see about that!
- You can do it, big brother!

181
00:09:42.433 --> 00:09:44.600
Pika! Pi!

182
00:09:44.666 --> 00:09:48.166
- Uh... Oh?
- What’s the matter?

183
00:09:48.233 --> 00:09:50.199
I’ve never fished before.

184
00:09:50.266 --> 00:09:53.566
- Oh, yeah? No prob! I’ll teach you.
- Oh, please!

185
00:09:53.633 --> 00:09:56.566
First, bring your rod all the way back like this,

186
00:09:56.633 --> 00:09:58.266
then fling it as far as you can.

187
00:09:58.333 --> 00:10:00.300
- Throw the lure!
- Like this?

188
00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:02.033
- Farther!
- How about this?

189
00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.866
Now you cast the lure with all your might!

190
00:10:07.533 --> 00:10:10.666
- Nice one!
- You definitely have potential!

191
00:10:10.733 --> 00:10:13.533
Wow, you think so?

192
00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:17.066
Hello there! It’s really nice to meet you!

193
00:10:17.133 --> 00:10:19.666
- Clauncher!
- Huh?

194
00:10:19.733 --> 00:10:21.900
- Oh.
- Na-na?

195
00:10:21.966 --> 00:10:24.400
Who’s that Pokémon?

196
00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:31.466
It’s Clauncher!

197
00:10:35.433 --> 00:10:38.199
- What’s that?
- A bite! Reel it in, quick!

198
00:10:38.266 --> 00:10:39.766
I’m trying!

199
00:10:39.833 --> 00:10:43.233
Oh! Could it be the giant golden Magikarp?

200
00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.166
We’ll give you a hand! Pull!

201
00:10:45.233 --> 00:10:47.166
Corsola!

202
00:10:47.233 --> 00:10:50.666
- Whoa. It’s a Corsola!
- It’s so cute!

203
00:10:50.733 --> 00:10:52.400
La Corsola!

204
00:10:52.466 --> 00:10:55.966
Serena, why don't you battle Corsola and catch it?

205
00:10:56.033 --> 00:10:59.400
If you want to catch it, you should battle it right away!

206
00:10:59.466 --> 00:11:03.199
Right! Okay, Fennekin, come on out!

207
00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.333
- Fennekin!
- Sola!

208
00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.100
Fenn! Fenn, Fenn, Fenn Fennekin!

209
00:11:10.166 --> 00:11:13.699
-Sol! La, La, La! Cors!

210
00:11:13.766 --> 00:11:15.933
You shouldn't have runaway like that, Fennekin!

211
00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.699
You should have battled instead!

212
00:11:17.766 --> 00:11:19.133
Fenn, Fenn, Fennekin!

213
00:11:19.199 --> 00:11:22.333
Well, it was all a bit sudden. Next time, for sure!

214
00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:23.699
Fennekin!

215
00:11:23.766 --> 00:11:25.500
Clauncher!

216
00:11:25.566 --> 00:11:29.800
- Want to play?
- Clauncher, Cher, Cher!

217
00:11:29.866 --> 00:11:31.866
- Huh?
- Na!

218
00:11:33.733 --> 00:11:35.733
- Cher!
- Na!

219
00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:37.800
- Na!
- Clauncher!

220
00:11:37.866 --> 00:11:39.666
Na! Na! Na! Na!

221
00:11:39.733 --> 00:11:41.666
Hey, stop fighting, both of you!

222
00:11:41.733 --> 00:11:45.100
-Wow! Dedenne! Stop it now!

223
00:11:45.166 --> 00:11:49.366
- Cher! Clauncher!
- Den, Den !

224
00:11:49.433 --> 00:11:50.466
Denne!

225
00:11:50.533 --> 00:11:54.266
Dedenne! Oh!

226
00:11:54.333 --> 00:11:55.966
Na. Na. Na. Na.

227
00:11:56.033 --> 00:11:58.033
Clauncher, now, you should know better

228
00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:00.699
than to attack an aquarium patron’s Pokémon!

229
00:12:00.766 --> 00:12:01.766
Cher!

230
00:12:01.833 --> 00:12:05.033
Clauncher could be a bit friendlier, I guess.

231
00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.100
It originally lived in the aquarium,

232
00:12:07.166 --> 00:12:10.900
so anyone who visited us here could watch and interact with it,

233
00:12:10.966 --> 00:12:13.733
but Clauncher didn’t like being looked at that way.

234
00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:18.199
It lost its appetite and I could tell it was getting sadder and sadder.

235
00:12:19.633 --> 00:12:23.000
So I decided to make it my Pokémon instead.

236
00:12:23.066 --> 00:12:25.766
Fortunately, it’s fine when it’s just the two of us.

237
00:12:25.833 --> 00:12:27.233
I see.

238
00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.066
- Claun!
- Dedenne!

239
00:12:32.199 --> 00:12:34.966
- Oh, you!
- Na! Na! Denne!

240
00:12:35.033 --> 00:12:38.033
Oh!

241
00:12:38.099 --> 00:12:42.033
Bonnie? I told you Dedenne’s Nuzzle was dangerous. Remember?

242
00:12:42.099 --> 00:12:44.633
Sorry. My brain’s numb.

243
00:12:44.699 --> 00:12:48.599
There! Our giant golden Magikarpbot is complete!

244
00:12:48.666 --> 00:12:50.133
The big lug gets three stars!

245
00:12:50.199 --> 00:12:54.233
The real golden Magikarp will think it’s a friend and approach it and then...

246
00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.433
Gotcha!

247
00:13:01.766 --> 00:13:04.833
Hey, Clemont. What are you making there, anyway?

248
00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:06.400
- All done!
- Huh?

249
00:13:06.466 --> 00:13:12.133
The future is now, thanks to science! Clemontic Gear on! Its name?

250
00:13:12.199 --> 00:13:16.900
The No Need For Water-type Pokémon Food Chinchou Model Magikarp Magnet!

251
00:13:16.966 --> 00:13:19.900
Your names are pretty boring, but they say it all.

252
00:13:19.966 --> 00:13:23.766
A sound wave inaudible to people will emit from Chinchou’s antennae

253
00:13:23.833 --> 00:13:25.900
all the way down to the bottom of the ocean.

254
00:13:25.966 --> 00:13:29.166
That sound wave has a naturally soothing effect on Magikarp,

255
00:13:29.233 --> 00:13:32.633
so they’ll be attracted to and gather around my wonderful device!

256
00:13:32.699 --> 00:13:35.533
And that’s when we'll reel them all in!

257
00:13:35.599 --> 00:13:38.433
Wow! Science is so amazing!

258
00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.633
- You’re a genius!
- Aw shucks. You flatter me!

259
00:13:41.699 --> 00:13:44.400
Let’s get to it! Power on!

260
00:13:50.133 --> 00:13:53.266
Do you really think that thing will work?

261
00:13:53.333 --> 00:13:54.666
Huh?

262
00:13:54.733 --> 00:13:58.833
- Is that a Magikarp?
- I don’t think so!

263
00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.733
- It’s a Sharpedo!
- Yargh!

264
00:14:11.833 --> 00:14:14.966
It didn’t work, in a big way.

265
00:14:15.033 --> 00:14:17.566
It shouldn’t have attracted them. Just Magikarp.

266
00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:26.433
You would think that glorious golden Magikarp would be all over us by now.

267
00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:29.400
-Heads up! Did you see that?

268
00:14:29.466 --> 00:14:31.933
- It was giant-size!
- Catching time!

269
00:14:33.933 --> 00:14:34.900
Yay!

270
00:14:39.666 --> 00:14:42.133
We swiped a Starmie instead!!

271
00:14:42.199 --> 00:14:44.666
- Then let it go!
- I’m trying!

272
00:14:50.366 --> 00:14:53.500
Fishing’s kind of boring when you don’t get any bites.

273
00:14:53.566 --> 00:14:56.400
But isn’t it nice to relax with nothing to do,

274
00:14:56.466 --> 00:15:00.199
with all the time in the world to feel the delightful ocean breezes?

275
00:15:00.266 --> 00:15:02.099
- All done!
- Huh?

276
00:15:02.166 --> 00:15:05.166
The future is still now, thanks to science!

277
00:15:05.233 --> 00:15:08.599
- It’s time for take two!
- Clemontic Gear on!

278
00:15:08.666 --> 00:15:14.033
Its name? The This Time It Will Attract Only Magikarp For Certain Lanturn Model!

279
00:15:14.099 --> 00:15:18.333
Your names are still pretty boring, but they do say it all, like them or not.

280
00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.699
You sure it’s going to work this time?

281
00:15:20.766 --> 00:15:24.866
Yes! I just ran extensive tests on the Magikarp in the aquarium

282
00:15:24.933 --> 00:15:27.233
and discovered which sound wave they prefer!

283
00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:28.333
Oh.

284
00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:31.599
This improved model will emit a special sound wave down to

285
00:15:31.666 --> 00:15:35.199
the bottom of the ocean, basically the same procedure as the Chinchou model!

286
00:15:35.266 --> 00:15:37.966
It’s amazing that science is so amazing!

287
00:15:38.033 --> 00:15:39.666
Let’s get started then.

288
00:15:39.733 --> 00:15:41.199
You’re sure about this?

289
00:15:41.266 --> 00:15:45.166
Golden Magikarp, come to me... now!

290
00:15:51.333 --> 00:15:54.266
Hm. Nothing seems to be happening.

291
00:15:55.599 --> 00:15:58.199
Oh! I’ve got a bite!

292
00:15:58.266 --> 00:16:01.466
- Yeah, so do I!
- I seem to have a bite, too!

293
00:16:01.533 --> 00:16:05.033
- All right! You can do it!
- Hey, I’ve got a bite!

294
00:16:07.766 --> 00:16:11.266
Huh? We’re being pulled backwards!

295
00:16:11.333 --> 00:16:13.500
- Meowth, what’s up?
- You got me!

296
00:16:13.566 --> 00:16:15.566
Pedal to the metal times ten!

297
00:16:18.966 --> 00:16:21.333
- So heavy!
- Mine’s heavy too!

298
00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:23.566
I’ve never caught something like this before!

299
00:16:23.633 --> 00:16:26.000
- Me neither!
- Hang on, Clemont!

300
00:16:26.066 --> 00:16:28.533
It’s too big for me to hold onto!

301
00:16:28.599 --> 00:16:31.000
Pika! Pika! Pika?

302
00:16:33.066 --> 00:16:35.066
- It’s huge!
- Humongous!

303
00:16:35.133 --> 00:16:37.366
Could we have caught it?

304
00:16:38.566 --> 00:16:40.900
We did! It’s the golden Magikarp!

305
00:16:40.966 --> 00:16:44.099
- Amazing! It really does exist!
- Pika!

306
00:16:44.166 --> 00:16:46.599
We really caught it! We really caught it!

307
00:16:46.666 --> 00:16:48.966
Excellent! My new device worked!

308
00:16:49.033 --> 00:16:51.166
- Great job, big brother!
- Claun!

309
00:16:51.233 --> 00:16:54.133
All right! Pikachu, are you ready to battle it?

310
00:16:54.199 --> 00:16:55.400
Pika, Pika!

311
00:16:56.666 --> 00:16:58.133
-Pika?

312
00:16:58.199 --> 00:16:59.266
No way!

313
00:16:59.333 --> 00:17:02.066
Prepare for trouble! No way, you say?

314
00:17:02.133 --> 00:17:04.333
And make it double! No way, no way!

315
00:17:04.399 --> 00:17:06.833
To protect the world from devastation!

316
00:17:06.899 --> 00:17:09.633
To unite all people within our nation!

317
00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:12.566
To denounce the evils of fishing hooks!

318
00:17:12.633 --> 00:17:16.133
To extend our denouncing to twerpish crooks!

319
00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.733
- Jessie!
- And James!

320
00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:21.333
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

321
00:17:21.399 --> 00:17:24.500
Surrender now or prepare for an aquatic fight!

322
00:17:24.566 --> 00:17:27.700
- Meowth, that’s right!
- Wobbuffet!

323
00:17:29.533 --> 00:17:31.000
Team Rocket!

324
00:17:31.066 --> 00:17:33.866
Can’t you see we’re trying to catch the golden Magikarp?

325
00:17:33.933 --> 00:17:36.233
Get yourself in someone else’s way for a change!

326
00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:37.533
Wobbuffet!

327
00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:40.399
Those guys are always messing everything up.

328
00:17:40.466 --> 00:17:41.766
Well, who are those guys?

329
00:17:41.833 --> 00:17:45.000
They’re bad guys who steal people’s Pokémon!

330
00:17:45.066 --> 00:17:49.233
Let’s grab those goons’ Pokémon and show them no one gets in Team Rocket’s face!

331
00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:50.933
Beginning with Clauncher!

332
00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.100
Down we go!

333
00:17:57.533 --> 00:17:58.966
Speedy Pokémon!

334
00:17:59.033 --> 00:18:01.466
Change up. Let’s set our sights on Dedenne!

335
00:18:01.533 --> 00:18:03.899
Na! Na! Na! Na!

336
00:18:03.966 --> 00:18:05.133
Dedenne! No!

337
00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.966
- Help Dedenne, Pikachu!
- Pikachu!

338
00:18:08.033 --> 00:18:10.933
Clauncher!

339
00:18:15.533 --> 00:18:17.766
Na! Na! Na! Na! Na! Huh?

340
00:18:17.833 --> 00:18:21.366
- Alley-oop, Pumpkaboo!
- You, too, Inkay!

341
00:18:23.966 --> 00:18:27.333
Use Shadow Ball!

342
00:18:27.399 --> 00:18:30.533
Look out, Clauncher! Dodge it!

343
00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:33.166
- Inkay, Psybeam!
- Inkay!

344
00:18:35.933 --> 00:18:39.500
- Now use Water Gun!
- Claun!

345
00:18:40.933 --> 00:18:43.000
Crabhammer, let’s go!

346
00:18:43.066 --> 00:18:45.833
Clauncher!

347
00:18:45.899 --> 00:18:48.200
- Now use Bubble Beam!
- Claun!

348
00:18:52.666 --> 00:18:54.133
- Oh!
- Pika! Pika! Pika!

349
00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.000
You’ve got it, buddy! Thunderbolt, go!

350
00:18:57.066 --> 00:19:01.100
Pikachu!

351
00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:05.933
We’re blasting off again!

352
00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:08.000
Wobbuffet!

353
00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:13.700
Thanks! That was so nice of you to rescue Dedenne!

354
00:19:13.766 --> 00:19:17.266
Clauncher may be a bit ornery, but it has a strong sense of justice.

355
00:19:17.333 --> 00:19:19.166
Clauncher!

356
00:19:25.066 --> 00:19:27.033
Guess it’s time to call it a day.

357
00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:30.200
I’m sorry for all the trouble you had to go through.

358
00:19:30.266 --> 00:19:32.033
And that we weren’t able to help much.

359
00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:34.533
Thank you for lending us your fishing rods.

360
00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:38.766
You kids go on and keep them. I’m certain they’ll come in handy someday.

361
00:19:38.833 --> 00:19:41.633
-Wow, really? Thank you so much!

362
00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:44.233
- We’ll take good care of them!
- We appreciate it!

363
00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:46.566
-Huh?

364
00:19:48.333 --> 00:19:52.266
Magikarp!

365
00:19:59.633 --> 00:20:01.633
Was... Was that it?

366
00:20:03.066 --> 00:20:04.800
Yeah!

367
00:20:04.866 --> 00:20:11.466
The legend is really true! Yes! it's true!

368
00:20:11.533 --> 00:20:12.866
- All right!
- Yeah!

369
00:20:12.933 --> 00:20:15.399
- It’s real!
- It does exist!

370
00:20:15.466 --> 00:20:18.700
Happy! Happy! Everybody’s happy!

371
00:20:22.766 --> 00:20:24.933
- Got to go.
- We’ll be back!

372
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:29.700
Good and I will have caught the golden Magikarp by the time I see you next!

373
00:20:29.766 --> 00:20:32.433
- We look forward to it!
- Na. Na. Na. Na!

374
00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:33.933
Clauncher!

375
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.300
Although our heroes were unable to help Rodman

376
00:20:36.366 --> 00:20:38.533
catch the golden Magikarp of legend,

377
00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.733
they’ve once again been reminded there are countless wonders

378
00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.899
they have yet to discover, as their exciting adventures continue!
